're all willing to  to to step up and play our part and and  i think the the harder part for us today  is we no longer have that sense  of solidarity with the rest of society  instead doctors in several provinces  feel at odds with policymakers  who are now balancing economic concerns  with the issues around public health we  really have a recipe of number one  psychological and emotional trauma and  number two  risk of them getting sick or being  quarantined according to the canadian  institute for health information more  than 21 000 health workers were infected  with culvin 19  during the country's first wave 12 of  those workers  died since then there have been another  915  infections among health workers in bc  more than 1800 in alberta  69 in saskatchewan 2096 in ontario  and more than 7 000 in quebec where  another 10 health workers have died  physicians  are tired the canadian medical  association says it's time for the  country to return to the mindset we had  last spring  so we're eight months into this pandemic  and canadians are  uh on the whole are are tired of hearing  about it um but the fact remains  that this is a virus that kills people  and we're seeing that now and with  hospitals in several parts of the  country  approaching capacity the need for a  fresh  sense of solidarity has never been so  great  heather urex west global news calgary  elon musk is questioning the accuracy of  covet 19 tests after testing positive  and negative in the same day the ceo of  tesla says something bogus is going on  after claiming he was tested four times  with different results  he tweeted two tests came back negative  two came back positive  same machine same test same nurse  musk took rapid antigen tests yesterday  and is now awaiting results from pcr  tests  the ones most commonly used in canada he  says he has symptoms  of a typical cold the miami marlins have  hired the league's first female and  first asian american gm  it's believed kim ing is the first 