ns  and buddhists worldwide  and one city ignored kova 19  restrictions to keep its guinness world  record  for most lights thousands of volunteers  lit over 584 000  oil lamps at many malls across this  country  the magical in-person experience with  saint nick will be replaced with a  virtual visit from santa's headquarters  in the north pole that's one holiday  tradition taking on a twist in 2020.  the prime minister says the way  canadians behave now will determine  how we can celebrate christmas and  there's a similar sentiment in europe  whereas redmond shannon reports there's  no guarantee of getting  home for the holidays  no one does christmas quite like the  germans but this year one traditional  market is more about  cars than carols  welcome to the drive-through christmas  market  this is as good as it gets when  everything else is closed  says this man a similar situation in  london  is dampening expectations for  celebrations  and i want as many londoners as possible  to have  a christmas although not like any other  christmas they've had before  but one that's semi-decent the promise  of a semi-decent festive season is a  deal that much of europe will have to  accept right now  the hope is that these november  lockdowns will be the key  to making that happen not objective  but france's prime minister says it's  still too early to be booking  any train tickets i think in terms of  people booking flights for christmas to  come home uh  i'd advise him not to do that at the  moment i know that's difficult i know  that's tough  a similar message in ireland i mean i'm  gonna be swimming  home if that's if that's what it comes  to i can't see them banning travel it's  not gonna be illegal  they're not going to be arresting people  at the airport immigrant ina quinn says  many people will travel no matter what  governments say  it just seems pretty wild that there's  no  plan in place you know there's a matter  of weeks to go now so  it's just really frustrating in canada  the holidays will also be different  but at least one thing has been  guaranteed by bc's top doctor  i think santa probably has immunity and  we'll look at how  we can facilitate him i think he'll be  washing his hands a lot and he probably  won't be eating cookies and milk  in every house this year but we'll find  ways of making it work  we're unlikely to ever forget christmas  2020  even if some of us will want to redmond  shannon global news  london and that is global national for  this friday i'm robin gill  we leave you tonight with the snow on  cypress mountain in british columbia  the popular resort reopened for the  winter season today of course there are  pandemic safety measures  for snowboarders and skiers thank you  for watching  i'll see you back here tomorrow have a  great night
 

